00:40:04,484 --> 00:40:07,464
So yeah, we really need to work on

476
00:40:07,944 --> 00:40:11,384
mobilizing data and large-scale digitization.

477
00:40:11,464 --> 00:40:15,044
And that's part of the mission of DiSSCo, to

478
00:40:15,504 --> 00:40:19,104
scale that up, to industrialize the digitization of the specimens,

479
00:40:19,704 --> 00:40:22,304
and to make that available as one homogenous,

480
00:40:23,224 --> 00:40:25,384
uniform dataset that you can use.

481
00:40:29,944 --> 00:40:33,104
So DiSSCo is a transformative infrastructure.

482
00:40:35,124 --> 00:40:35,684
So it

483
00:40:36,684 --> 00:40:40,144
synchronizes between all these scattered datasets,

484
00:40:41,704 --> 00:40:44,624
create one big European virtual collection,

485
00:40:45,904 --> 00:40:47,264
with FAIR-compliant data.

486
00:40:48,604 --> 00:40:52,564
So it's findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable, both by

487
00:40:52,604 --> 00:40:56,224
humans, but also by machines. And it's machine actionable, so

488
00:40:56,264 --> 00:40:59,864
machines can act upon the data, can enrich the data

489
00:40:59,944 --> 00:41:03,404
with linkages to derived and related data,

490
00:41:04,884 --> 00:41:08,244
like sequence information, literature, et cetera.

491
00:41:09,564 --> 00:41:09,824
So,

492
00:41:10,704 --> 00:41:14,264
we can connect the data or reconnect the data, the specimen data,

493
00:41:14,744 --> 00:41:17,483
with all that extra information that's available on the internet.

494
00:41:18,224 --> 00:41:19,984
And we can do it on a very large scale.

495
00:41:24,644 --> 00:41:28,564
And the core of the infrastructure is the DiSSCo Extended Specimen,

496
00:41:29,704 --> 00:41:32,324
which is an actionable and citable unit.

497
00:41:32,944 --> 00:41:34,664
