2300
03:02:04,958 --> 03:02:08,918
And this is the situation, except much more complicated in biodiversity.

2301
03:02:09,058 --> 03:02:12,658
Organisms are even less cooperative during biodiversity surveys.

2302
03:02:12,738 --> 03:02:16,718
They may remain quiet, hide, be cryptic, or

2303
03:02:16,778 --> 03:02:19,338
be otherwise temporarily unavailable for detection.

2304
03:02:26,018 --> 03:02:29,978
And so it leads you to think about what's going on here, and initial

2305
03:02:30,038 --> 03:02:30,638
thought was

2306
03:02:31,598 --> 03:02:35,238
that presence and absence is two sides of the same

2307
03:02:35,318 --> 03:02:36,518
coin. It's a pair.

2308
03:02:37,818 --> 03:02:40,518
But it's not. It's really asymmetric,

2309
03:02:41,438 --> 03:02:42,238
and that's because

2310
03:02:44,358 --> 03:02:47,838
presence is a fact, while absence is a question.

2311
03:02:48,618 --> 03:02:51,998
It seems unbounded. It doesn't seem like there's really an answer.

2312
03:02:53,798 --> 03:02:57,098
And for instance, a missing data point, a null value, is inherently

2313
03:02:57,158 --> 03:03:01,078
ill-defined. Did the sensor break? Did the event not occur?

2314
03:03:01,498 --> 03:03:03,898
Was the datum simply not recorded?

2315
03:03:08,938 --> 03:03:12,838
In data analysis, we have the recent concept of expectation

2316
03:03:12,938 --> 03:03:16,818
frames. This is from a new paper. But it's something that

2317
03:03:16,878 --> 03:03:20,538
we understood before. It just hasn't been written about to my knowledge.

2318
03:03:21,458 --> 03:03:25,298
We quote from the paper, "Absence is meaningful only against a model

2319
03:03:25,718 --> 03:03:29,658
of what should have been present. It is not a signal on

2320
03:03:29,698 --> 03:03:32,418
its own, but a deviation from expectation."

2321
03:03:33,382 --> 03:03:37,142
And so in ecological surveys, that expectation frame is

2322
03:03:37,222 --> 03:03:39,702
set by having a survey target.

2323
03:03:40,882 --> 03:03:44,742
And you can see the Darwin Core management conceptual

2324
03:03:44,842 --> 03:03:48,822
model, and then an absence is no longer unbounded,

2325
03:03:48,922 --> 03:03:49,722
and its meaning

2326
03:03:50,842 --> 03:03:54,462
as an undetected target can be assigned a zero count.

2327
03:03:55,162 --> 03:03:58,922
And here's what the Humboldt Core extension says about

2328
03:03:59,002 --> 03:03:59,322
that.

2329
03:04:00,942 --> 03:04:02,802
We have defined a survey target,

2330
03:04:03,902 --> 03:04:07,702
and its scope is one or more scopes that

2331
03:04:08,062 --> 03:04:10,242
describe a target for the occurrences.

2332
03:04:11,462 --> 03:04:15,122
It could be something like all the bird species, all the bird species except

2333
03:04:15,882 --> 03:04:17,862
some gulls and kittiwakes. It could be

2334
03:04:18,942 --> 03:04:20,062
whatever you define.

2335
03:04:21,102 --> 03:04:24,982
There are two salmon species in that last line

2336
03:04:25,022 --> 03:04:25,222
there.

2337
03:04:27,722 --> 03:04:30,982
One of my early ideas was that perhaps books about

2338
03:04:32,182 --> 03:04:34,722
survey methodology would be helpful.

2339
03:04:35,562 --> 03:04:38,222
Here are a list of books that I looked at

2340
03:04:39,022 --> 03:04:39,782
and searched

2341
03:04:41,282 --> 03:04:44,702
by looking in the appendix and looking for presence and absence and

2342
03:04:44,762 --> 03:04:48,442
detection and related terms. Or later, I got electronic

2343
03:04:48,502 --> 03:04:50,042
versions and looked

2344
03:04:51,622 --> 03:04:53,522
using the computer. And

2345
